-# Verilog Agent · Counter MVP · Private VM acceptance patch
+# Verilog Agent — Counter MVP (trusted verdict)
 
-**Scope:** Synchronous 4-bit reset/enable counter ONLY. UART/FIFO/FSM remain unimplemented. Vultr Serverless Inference generates candidate `dut.v` (or `MOCK_LLM=1` returns canned RTL). The only verification decision is issued by `trusted/verdict.py`, comparing 87 frozen observations from a fixed testbench with a host oracle. The LLM never supplies the TB/oracle or a PASS verdict.
+## Status and scope
 
-**Security caveat:** The entire app/backend can talk to a Docker daemon via a socket. The fixed-argument wrapper and Docker sandbox restrictions reduce risk, but a compromised backend may access the daemon. **This package is only for a private, operator-authenticated, isolated VM accessible through SSH port forwarding.** It is not a public hardened service and is not a security proof that the blast radius is literally zero.
+Only `counter4_sync_v1` is implemented. Vultr Serverless Inference can propose `dut.v` in a **private operator-only** deployment; trusted host `verdict.py` and fixed `tb_counter.sv` exclusively determine PASS/FAIL. `MOCK_LLM=1` exercises canned example RTL and an intentional bad-enable self-heal sequence; **MOCK is never live Vultr evidence**. UART/FIFO/FSM are not implemented.
 
-## No-Vultr, no-Docker tests (already run for this patch)
+**This is not an audited public general-purpose RTL service.** The limited counter vectors do not establish formal correctness. Public demo mode is fixed MOCK cases only, not user code.
+
